SUMMARY:Dance! with Arts for Autism (Ages 3-10)
DESCRIPTION:Join us the second Tuesday of the month for a fun dance program 
 hosted by Arts for Autism. Led by Keri Small\, these sessions are a fun way 
 to explore movement\, get some wiggles out\, and make new 
 friends.\n\nPreK-5th Grade Session (ages 3-10): 4:00-4:30pm\n\n6th to 10th 
 Grade Session (ages 11-15): 4:40-5:10pm\n\nRegistration is encouraged but 
 not required. Caregivers are required to stay with children ages 10 and 
 younger.\n\nArts for Autism is a 501(c)3 nonprofit organization dedicated 
 to creating inclusive\, equitable\, and intentional arts based learning 
 opportunities to children and adolescents on the spectrum. They have hosted 
 events all across North Carolina\, and are excited to continue programming 
 at a library near you!\n
LOCATION:Main Children's Programming Room\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Accessibility Services":MAILTO:accessibility_services@dconc.gov
