SUMMARY:Employment Essentials - Email Basics
DESCRIPTION:\na {\n    text-decoration: none\;\n    color: #464feb\;\n}\ntr 
 th\, tr td {\n    border: 1px solid #e6e6e6\;\n}\ntr th {\n    
 background-color: #f5f5f5\;\n}\n\n\n\nPart of the Employment Essentials 
 workshop series\, this beginner‑friendly workshop is designed for 
 individuals ages 35-60 who are new to using email or who need a 
 confidence‑boosting refresher in skills essential for job searching\, 
 professional communication\, and everyday digital life.\n\nParticipants 
 will learn:\n\n\n	What email is and how it works\n	How to create and 
 navigate an email account\n	How to read\, write\, and send messages\n	How 
 to attach documents and photos\n	How to recognize safe vs. suspicious 
 emails\n	Tips for organizing your inbox and managing messages\n	Simple 
 habits to protect your privacy and security\n\n\nBy the end of the 
 session\, attendees will feel more confident communicating online and using 
 email for personal\, professional\, and employment‑related tasks.\n\n 
 \n\nAttend 3 sessions of this workshop series to earn a free headshot photo 
 from a professional photographer.
LOCATION:Bragtown Branch Library (3200 Dearborn Dr)
ORGANIZER;CN="Austin Daniels":MAILTO:ausdaniels@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Career Development, Digital/Tech Literacy
UID:LibCal-14288-17363762
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17363762
END:VEVENT
